## API Documentation

All endpoints are prefixed with:

```
/api
```

All requests and responses use **JSON**.

---

## Authentication

### Register

**Endpoint**

```
POST /api/register
```

**Request Body**

```json
{
  "name": "John Doe",
  "email": "john@example.com",
  "password": "password",
  "password_confirmation": "password"
}
```

**Response (201)**

```json
{
  "user": {
    "id": 1,
    "name": "John Doe",
    "email": "john@example.com"
  },
  "token": {
    "access_token": "eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGci...",
    "token_type": "Bearer"
  }
}
```

---

### Login

```
POST /api/login
```

**Request Body**

```json
{
  "email": "john@example.com",
  "password": "password"
}
```

**Response (200)**

```json
{
  "access_token": "eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGci...",
  "token_type": "Bearer"
}
```

---

### Logout (Authenticated)

```
POST /api/logout
```

**Headers**

```
Authorization: Bearer {access_token}
```

**Response**

```json
{
  "message": "Logged out successfully"
}
```

---

### Get Authenticated User

```
GET /api/me
```

**Headers**

```
Authorization: Bearer {access_token}
```

**Response**

```json
{
  "id": 1,
  "name": "John Doe",
  "email": "john@example.com",
  "role": "customer"
}
```

